const faqs = [
  { q: 'What condition does furniture need to be in to donate?', a: 'Donated furniture must be in usable condition — structurally sound, clean and free of significant damage or stains. Upholstered items (sofas, armchairs, mattresses) must have their fire safety labels attached, as required by the Furniture and Furnishings (Fire Safety) Regulations 1988. Items with missing labels cannot legally be resold or given away.' },
  { q: 'Will charities collect furniture from my home?', a: 'Yes, most Bristol furniture charities offer free collection for larger items like sofas, beds, wardrobes and tables. The SOFA Project, Emmaus Bristol and the British Heart Foundation all collect from Bristol postcodes. You\'ll typically need to book a few days ahead, and items must be accessible from a ground-floor door.' },
  { q: 'What if my furniture isn\'t good enough to donate?', a: 'If furniture is too worn or damaged for donation, you still have options. Bristol recycling centres accept furniture for free. Council bulky waste collection costs £35 for up to 3 items. Or a professional clearance service like Clearfields will collect from any room and ensure responsible disposal, recycling what we can.' },
];
